      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-19811",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/58/5877e86c201ae9cbc9912b3fcc810fd2283ac1ff2448ddcb1cc37f26c7412a3e.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed by the curve $x =-\\sqrt{9 - y^{2}}$ and the $y$-axis for $-3 \\le y \\le 0$, as shown in the picture. Given that cross-sections perpendicular to the $y$-axis are quarter-circles, calculate the volume of the solid."
